Feeling nervous, anxious, or on edge.evidence:
There's the way the dust motes dance in the afternoon sun when it hits my kitchen window.

Before... well, before I started really listening to that hum and noticing these small things, if I saw a speck of dust floating in the light, my brain would immediately zoom in on it. It would make me think, *Did someone walk by? Is there an intruder? What if they're standing right there behind that speck?* My heart would hammer so fast I'd feel dizzy, and I'd have to turn away quickly.

But lately? When the sun hits just right and those little brown particles start swirling in the beam, I don't panic anymore. I just watch them. They move slowly, drifting up and down, never stopping, never trying to fix anything. And as I watch them, that same low hum in my chest gets even quieter, more steady. It feels like the dust isn't an intruder;

